            <ArticleTitle>Melorheostosis of the tenth and eleventh thoracic vertebrae crossing the facet joint: a rare cause of back pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>283-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Melorheostosis affecting the axial skeleton is a rare condition. We present a case affecting a single thoracic zygoapophyseal (facet) joint that proved to be a diagnostic challenge. CT, MRI and radionuclide imaging with surgical and histopathology findings are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
